{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>That which Elohim, etc.</b> It may be explained along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Berakhot 55a): three things the Holy One, blessed be He, proclaims, and they are: abundance, famine, and a provider. And His saying ״אֵת אֲשֶׁר הָאֱלֹהִים עֹשֶׂה״ — in His own honor, not through an agent — ״הִגִּיד״ etc.: abundance — these are the two of abundance; famine — these are the two of famine; a provider — ״יֵרֶא פַרְעֹה אִישׁ״ etc. And although he did not tell him who this man is, nevertheless afterward the truth supported his lot, in that He withheld the interpretation from all his wise men and revealed Joseph to him through the chief butler who told him what had happened to him, and the matters came round and Joseph was revealed to him, ״וַיְשִׁיתֵהוּ עַל אֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם״. And His saying <b>הִגִּיד לְפַרְעֹה</b> — meaning that there is an opportunity in his hand to make a remedy, as he said at the end (Genesis 41:33): ״יֵרֶא פַרְעֹה״ etc. ״וְחִמֵּשׁ״ etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:31.352687453Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}